From: kschen <admin@kschen.eu.org>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 21:14:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] media: venus: hfi_cmds: pack H264_TRANSFORM_8X8 in the 1x
 packetizer

venc_set_properties() sets HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_H264_TRANSFORM_8X8
(0x2005025) for every H.264 encode session, but that property is only
handled by pkt_session_set_property_4xx()/_6xx().  On HFI_VERSION_1XX and
HFI_VERSION_3XX the 3xx packetizer falls through to
pkt_session_set_property_1x(), which has no case for it and hits
"default: return -EINVAL".

The error propagates back through venc_set_properties() into
venc_queue_setup(), so VIDIOC_REQBUFS fails with -EINVAL and hardware
H.264 encoding is unusable on every HFI 3XX SoC.  VP8, HEVC, MPEG4 and
H263 encoding are unaffected because the property is only set inside the
H.264 branch.

Diagnosed on a Xiaomi Mi 5s (msm8996 pro, Venus hw 3.43.15, firmware
VIDEO.VE.4.4-00040): ftrace function_graph on venc_queue_setup() shows the
fifth hfi_session_set_property() call returning without ever reaching
venus_iface_cmdq_write(), and disassembling venus-enc.ko confirms that
call carries ptype 0x02005025.

The packet layout is a single u32, identical to the 4xx one, so add the
case to the 1x packetizer.  It goes before the "NOT IMPLEMENTED IN CORE
YET" fallthrough list so that none of those labels get captured by it.

Tested: 640x480 and 1280x720 H.264 High profile encode now produce valid
streams; hardware decode and the other encoders are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: kschen <admin@kschen.eu.org>
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
index 3ae0630..d691cc8 100755
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
@@ -1064,6 +1064,13 @@ static int pkt_session_set_property_1x(struct hfi_session_set_property_pkt *pkt,
 		pkt->shdr.hdr.size += sizeof(u32) + sizeof(*info);
 		break;
 	}
+	case HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_H264_TRANSFORM_8X8: {
+		struct hfi_h264_8x8_transform *in = pdata, *tm = prop_data;
+
+		tm->enable_type = in->enable_type;
+		pkt->shdr.hdr.size += sizeof(u32) + sizeof(*tm);
+		break;
+	}
 	case HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_HDR10_PQ_SEI:
 		return -ENOTSUPP;
 
